{
 "about": "Every OBP-API call Hola makes: verb, path (OBP placeholders in capitals), the source file and the text that makes the call (needles: the @Value URL and where it is used, which gives the verb), and the response fields the code reads, in Java or in the page scripts the body is passed to. calls are the OBP-API calls; obp-api-contract/snapshot.py writes snapshot.json for them from an OBP-API's resource docs. standard_calls are the UK Open Banking and Berlin Group calls, which have no OBP resource docs, so only their place in the source is checked. declared_but_unused are @Value URLs no code uses. src/test/java/com/openbankproject/hydra/auth/ObpApiContractTest.java checks all of this offline.",
